IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`
IMPORT `sfa-interests`
IMPORT `sfaa-div1-interpretation`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, Part 7 Division 3 (sections 137S to 137X): disclosure of interests in a real estate investment trust and in the shares of its responsible person, first half.
-- Section 137U applies sections 135 to 137B to substantial unitholders of a real estate investment trust "with such modifications and qualifications as may be necessary":
-- the functions of sfaa-div1-shareholders are called with the trust standing where the corporation stood (the caller answers `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)`
-- from `s 137S the trust is a real estate investment trust within Division 3`), the notified body being "the trustee" and "the responsible person", and the substantial
-- unitholder where the substantial shareholder stood. The sections that mirror Division 1 are generated from Division 1's sources with the words changed and the text of THIS
-- Division quoted.

§ `s 137S: application and interpretation of Division 3`

-- src:29934 | 137S.—(1) This section has effect for the purposes of this Division
-- src:29935 | but does not affect the operation of any other provision of this Act.
@ref s 137S(1) (src:29934-29935)
GIVEN
    `the provision being read is in Division 3 of Part 7` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision being read one in Division 3 of Part 7 of the Act (sections 137S to 137ZC)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137S(1) section 137S has effect for the purposes of Division 3 and does not affect any other provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision being read is in Division 3 of Part 7`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not affect the operation of any other provision of this Act"


-- Subsection (2): "real estate investment trust" means a collective investment scheme that is a trust, invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets the
-- Authority specifies in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes, and has units listed by way of a primary listing. What the Code specifies is not in the text, so it is an input.
-- src:29944 | “real estate investment trust” means a collective investment
-- src:29945 | scheme that is a trust, that invests primarily in real estate and
-- src:29946 | real estate‑related assets specified by the Authority in the
-- src:29947 | Code on Collective Investment Schemes, and any or all the
-- src:29948 | units in which are listed, by way of a primary listing, for
-- src:29949 | quotation on the official list of an approved exchange;
@ref s 137S(2) "real estate investment trust" (src:29944-29949)
GIVEN
    `the scheme is a collective investment scheme that is a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme a collective investment scheme that is a trust?
    `the scheme invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the scheme invest primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes?
    `any or all of the units in the scheme are listed by way of a primary listing for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any or all of the units in the scheme listed, by way of a primary listing, for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137S(2) the scheme is a real estate investment trust` MEANS
    IF `the scheme is a collective investment scheme that is a trust` AND `the scheme invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes` AND `any or all of the units in the scheme are listed by way of a primary listing for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“real estate investment trust” means a collective investment scheme that is a trust, that invests primarily in real estate and real estate‑related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes, and any or all the units in which are listed, by way of a primary listing, for quotation on the official list of an approved exchange"

-- src:29951 | “trustee” means —
-- src:29953 | (a) in relation to a real estate investment trust authorised
-- src:29954 | under section 286, the trustee approved under
-- src:29955 | section 289 for the trust; and
@ref s 137S(2) "trustee" (a) (src:29951-29955)
GIVEN
    `the real estate investment trust is authorised under section 286` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the real estate investment trust authorised under section 286?
    `the person is the trustee approved under section 289 for the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the trustee approved under section 289 for the trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137S(2) "trustee" (a) the person is the trustee of an authorised real estate investment trust` MEANS
    IF `the real estate investment trust is authorised under section 286` AND `the person is the trustee approved under section 289 for the trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a real estate investment trust authorised under section 286, the trustee approved under section 289 for the trust"

-- src:29951 | “trustee” means —
-- src:29953 | (a) in relation to a real estate investment trust authorised
-- src:29954 | under section 286, the trustee approved under
-- src:29955 | section 289 for the trust; and
-- src:29957 | (b) in relation to any other real estate investment trust, an
-- src:29958 | entity equivalent to a trustee referred to in
-- src:29959 | paragraph (a).
@ref s 137S(2) "trustee" (b) (src:29951-29959)
GIVEN
    `the real estate investment trust is authorised under section 286` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the real estate investment trust authorised under section 286?
    `the person is an entity equivalent to a trustee approved under section 289` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an entity equivalent to a trustee approved under section 289?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137S(2) "trustee" (b) the person is the trustee of any other real estate investment trust` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the real estate investment trust is authorised under section 286`) AND `the person is an entity equivalent to a trustee approved under section 289`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to any other real estate investment trust, an entity equivalent to a trustee referred to in paragraph (a)"

-- Either paragraph is enough; both no is the text's no; a limb the caller could not answer is not read as a no.
-- src:29951 | “trustee” means —
-- src:29953 | (a) in relation to a real estate investment trust authorised
-- src:29954 | under section 286, the trustee approved under
-- src:29955 | section 289 for the trust; and
-- src:29957 | (b) in relation to any other real estate investment trust, an
-- src:29958 | entity equivalent to a trustee referred to in
-- src:29959 | paragraph (a).
@ref s 137S(2) "trustee" (src:29951-29959)
GIVEN
    `the person is the trustee of the real estate investment trust within paragraph (a) of section 137S(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 137S(2) paragraph (a) answer for the person (the approved trustee of an authorised trust)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person is the trustee of the real estate investment trust within paragraph (b) of section 137S(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 137S(2) paragraph (b) answer for the person (an entity equivalent to such a trustee)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137S(2) "trustee" the person is the trustee of the real estate investment trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the person is the trustee of the real estate investment trust within paragraph (a) of section 137S(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person is the trustee of the real estate investment trust within paragraph (b) of section 137S(2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`the person is the trustee of the real estate investment trust within paragraph (a) of section 137S(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the person is the trustee of the real estate investment trust within paragraph (b) of section 137S(2)` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“trustee” means"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a limb the caller could not answer is not read as a no

-- Subsection (3): "To avoid doubt, section 4 applies". The keel's s 4 is called, not restated. Division 3 speaks of "securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units
-- in a collective investment scheme", so the thing may be any of the three; a thing that is none of them is outside the sentence.
-- src:29963 | (3) To avoid doubt, section 4 applies for the purpose of determining
-- src:29964 | whether a person has an interest in securities, securities‑based
-- src:29965 | derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme under
-- src:29966 | this Division.
@ref s 137S(3) (src:29963-29966)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a security, a securities-based derivatives contract or a unit in a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a security, a securities-based derivatives contract or a unit in a collective investment scheme (as section 2(1) defines those)?
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(1) answer (authority to dispose of, or control the disposal of, the thing)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(3) answer (a trust)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(4) answer (a corporation the person directs or controls)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(5) answer (a corporation in which the person and associates hold 20% of the votes)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(7)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(7) answer (one of the circumstances in subsection (7))? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(8)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for s 4(8) answer (joint holding)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the interest is to be disregarded under section 4(10)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does `s 4(10) the interest is to be disregarded` answer for this interest? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137S(3) the person has an interest in the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units under Division 3` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a security, a securities-based derivatives contract or a unit in a collective investment scheme`
    THEN `s 4 the person has an interest in the securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units` TRUE `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(1)` `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(3)` `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(4)` `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(5)` `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(7)` `the person has an interest by the route of s 4(8)` `the interest is to be disregarded under section 4(10)`
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "whether a person has an interest in securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme under this Division"

-- src:29970 | (4) Section 130(6) and (7) applies for the purposes of —
-- src:29972 | (a) sections 135(2)(b), 136(1) and 137(1) as applied by
-- src:29973 | section 137U(1); and
-- src:29975 | (b) sections 137W(6), 137Y(2)(b)(i), 137ZA(1) and
-- src:29976 | 137ZC(1),
@ref s 137S(4) (src:29970-29976)
GIVEN
    `the provision being read is one of sections 135(2)(b), 136(1) and 137(1) as applied by section 137U(1), and 137W(6), 137Y(2)(b)(i), 137ZA(1) and 137ZC(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision being read one of sections 135(2)(b), 136(1) and 137(1) as applied by section 137U(1), or section 137W(6), 137Y(2)(b)(i), 137ZA(1) or 137ZC(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137S(4) section 130(6) and (7) apply to the provision` MEANS
    IF `the provision being read is one of sections 135(2)(b), 136(1) and 137(1) as applied by section 137U(1), and 137W(6), 137Y(2)(b)(i), 137ZA(1) and 137ZC(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Section 130(6) and (7) applies for the purposes of"; a provision it does not list is outside it

§ `s 137T: who must comply with Division 3, and the Authority's exemption and extension`

-- src:29986 | 137T.—(1) The obligation to comply with this Division extends to
-- src:29987 | all natural persons, whether resident in Singapore or not and whether
-- src:29992 | citizens of Singapore or not, and to all entities, whether formed,
-- src:29993 | constituted or carrying on business in Singapore or not.
@ref s 137T(1) (src:29986-29993)
GIVEN
    `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a natural person?
    `the person is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an entity (as section 2(1) defines "entity")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137T(1) the obligation to comply with Division 3 extends to the person` MEANS
    -- Residence in Singapore and citizenship are immaterial ("whether resident in Singapore or not and whether citizens of Singapore or not"), so neither is an input.
    IF `the person is a natural person` OR `the person is an entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names "all natural persons" and "all entities"; a person who is neither is not addressed

-- src:29997 | (2) This Division extends to acts done or omitted to be done outside
-- src:29998 | Singapore.
@ref s 137T(2) (src:29997-29998)
GIVEN
    `the act or omission was done or omitted to be done outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the act done, or the thing omitted, outside Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137T(2) Division 3 extends to the act or omission` MEANS
    IF `the act or omission was done or omitted to be done outside Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This Division extends to acts done or omitted to be done outside Singapore"; an act in Singapore is not this subsection's subject

-- src:30002 | (3) The Authority may exempt any person or class of persons from
-- src:30003 | any or all of the provisions of this Division.
@ref s 137T(3) (src:30002-30003)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has exempted the person, or a class of persons including the person, from the provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority exempted the person, or a class of persons that includes the person, from the provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137T(3) the person is exempt from the provision of Division 3` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has exempted the person, or a class of persons including the person, from the provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "The Authority may exempt any person or class of persons from any or all of the provisions of this Division"; whether it has done so is the Authority's act

-- src:30007 | (4) The Authority may by written notice impose on a person
-- src:30008 | exempted under subsection (3), or by regulations impose on a class of
-- src:30009 | persons exempted under that subsection, such conditions or
-- src:30010 | restrictions as the Authority thinks fit and the person or persons
-- src:30011 | must comply with such conditions or restrictions.
@ref s 137T(4) (src:30007-30011)
GIVEN
    `the person is exempted under section 137T(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority exempted the person under section 137T(3)?
    `the Authority has imposed a condition or restriction on the person by written notice, or on the class of persons by regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority imposed a condition or restriction on the person by written notice, or on a class of persons including the person by regulations?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137T(4) the exempted person must comply with the condition or restriction` MEANS
    IF `the person is exempted under section 137T(3)` AND `the Authority has imposed a condition or restriction on the person by written notice, or on the class of persons by regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person exempted under subsection (3)" with a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (4)

DECLARE `s 137T action` IS ONE OF
    `s 137T contravene a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (4)`

-- s 137T(4) is a "must comply" with no time limit, so as a MUST it has no breach path (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path"); the same duty is written as the
-- prohibition it amounts to (SHANT, derived from the flat negative: ruling N2 of 2026-11-04) so that a trace can reach the offence of subsection (5).
-- src:30007 | (4) The Authority may by written notice impose on a person
-- src:30008 | exempted under subsection (3), or by regulations impose on a class of
-- src:30009 | persons exempted under that subsection, such conditions or
-- src:30010 | restrictions as the Authority thinks fit and the person or persons
-- src:30011 | must comply with such conditions or restrictions.
-- src:30015 | (5) Any person who contravenes any condition or restriction
-- src:30016 | imposed under subsection (4) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:30017 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in
-- src:30018 | the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding
-- src:30019 | $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence
-- src:30020 | continues after conviction.
@ref s 137T(4) and (5) (the prohibition) (src:30007-30020)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137T action`
`s 137T(4) and (5) the exempted person shall not contravene a condition or restriction` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "the exempted person"
    SHANT `s 137T contravene a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (4)`
    LEST BREACH BY Individual "the exempted person" BECAUSE "contravened a condition or restriction imposed under section 137T(4): an offence under section 137T(5)"

-- src:30015 | (5) Any person who contravenes any condition or restriction
-- src:30016 | imposed under subsection (4) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:30017 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in
-- src:30018 | the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding
-- src:30019 | $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence
-- src:30020 | continues after conviction.
@ref s 137T(5) (src:30015-30020)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under section 137T(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene a condition or restriction imposed under section 137T(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137T(5) the person is guilty of an offence of contravening a condition or restriction` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under section 137T(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("Any person who contravenes any condition or restriction"), not that a person who does not is innocent

-- src:30015 | (5) Any person who contravenes any condition or restriction
-- src:30016 | imposed under subsection (4) shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:30017 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in
-- src:30018 | the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding
-- src:30019 | $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence
-- src:30020 | continues after conviction.
@ref 2 s 137T(5) (the penalty) (src:30015-30020)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 137T(5) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, for a continuing offence, a further fine not exceeding $5,000 a day after conviction; no imprisonment is stated, so 0
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000

-- s 137T(6): the Authority may extend the time, on application. The "may" is gated by "on the application of a person required to give a notice":
-- the grant-and-power ruling (the grant limit) says NOTHING when the gate fails; the periods ruling (b) would say JUST FALSE. SPLIT-SITE (ii), fork line B2.
-- src:30024 | (6) The Authority may, on the application of a person required to
-- src:30025 | give a notice under this Division, extend, or further extend, the time
-- src:30026 | for giving the notice.
@ref s 137T(6) (src:30024-30026)
GIVEN
    `a person required to give a notice under Division 3 has applied to the Authority for an extension of the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person required to give a notice under Division 3 applied to the Authority to extend the time for giving the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137T(6) the Authority has power to extend, or further extend, the time for giving the notice` MEANS
    IF `a person required to give a notice under Division 3 has applied to the Authority for an extension of the time`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (ii) "may, on the application of a person required to give a notice under this Division"; the gate is not a "where" and the function is named for a power

-- src:30024 | (6) The Authority may, on the application of a person required to
-- src:30025 | give a notice under this Division, extend, or further extend, the time
-- src:30026 | for giving the notice.
@ref 2 s 137T(6) (the last day after an extension) (src:30024-30026)
GIVEN
    `the last day for giving the notice under the section` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for giving the notice under the section (before any extension)?
    `the Authority has extended the time on the person's application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority, on the person's application, extended the time for giving the notice?
    `the last day to which the Authority has extended the time` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day to which the Authority has extended the time (leave any date if there is no extension)?
GIVETH A DATE
`s 137T(6) the last day for giving the notice, as extended on the person's application` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has extended the time on the person's application` AND (`the last day to which the Authority has extended the time` GREATER THAN `the last day for giving the notice under the section`)
    THEN `the last day to which the Authority has extended the time`
    ELSE `the last day for giving the notice under the section`


-- s 137TA (the Authority's power to extend the scope of Division 3 by regulations): a regulation-making power, so a coverage row `inert` (reason 2), no code.

§ `s 137U: duty of a substantial unitholder to notify the trustee and the responsible person of interests`

-- src:30076 | 137U.—(1) Sections 135 to 137B apply, with such modifications
-- src:30077 | and qualifications as may be necessary, to a person who is a
-- src:30078 | substantial unitholder of a real estate investment trust as though —
-- src:30080 | (a) references to the corporation to which notification should
-- src:30081 | be given were references to —
-- src:30083 | (i) the trustee of the real estate investment trust; and
-- src:30085 | (ii) the responsible person for the real estate investment
-- src:30086 | trust;
-- src:30091 | (b) references to shares or voting shares in the corporation
-- src:30092 | were references to units or voting units in the real estate
-- src:30093 | investment trust; and
-- src:30095 | (c) references to a substantial shareholder in the corporation
-- src:30096 | were references to a substantial unitholder of the real estate
-- src:30097 | investment trust,
-- src:30099 | and such person must comply with those provisions accordingly.
@ref s 137U(1) (src:30076-30099)
GIVEN
    `the trust is a real estate investment trust within section 137S` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trust a real estate investment trust as section 137S(2) defines it?
    `the person is a substantial unitholder of the real estate investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a substantial unitholder of the real estate investment trust (as section 2(1) defines "substantial unitholder")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137U(1) sections 135 to 137B apply to the substantial unitholder` MEANS
    IF `the trust is a real estate investment trust within section 137S` AND `the person is a substantial unitholder of the real estate investment trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a person who is a substantial unitholder of a real estate investment trust"

-- src:30103 | (2) Any person to whom subsection (1) applies who —
-- src:30105 | (a) intentionally or recklessly contravenes section 135, 136(1)
-- src:30106 | or (2), 137, 137A or 137B as applied by subsection (1); or
-- src:30108 | (b) in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or
-- src:30109 | 137B as applied by subsection (1), provides any
-- src:30110 | information which the person knows is false or
-- src:30111 | misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to
-- src:30112 | whether it is,
-- src:30114 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall —
-- src:30116 | (c) in the case of an individual, be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:30117 | not exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:30118 | exceeding 2 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:30119 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $25,000 for every
-- src:30120 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues
-- src:30121 | after conviction; or
-- src:30123 | (d) in the case of a corporation, be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:30124 | not exceeding $250,000 and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:30125 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $25,000 for every
-- src:30126 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues
-- src:30127 | after conviction.
@ref s 137U(2) (src:30103-30127)
GIVEN
    `the person contravened section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B as applied by section 137U(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person contravene section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B as applied by section 137U(1)?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B as applied by section 137U(1) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B as applied by section 137U(1), did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137U(2) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF ((`the person contravened section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B as applied by section 137U(1)` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`) OR (`the person in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B as applied by section 137U(1) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("intentionally or recklessly contravenes section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B as applied by subsection (1)" or "provides any information which the person knows is false or misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is"), not that anyone else is innocent

@ref s 137U(2) (the penalty) (src:30103-30127)
GIVEN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 137U(2) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an individual`
        THEN JUST (Penalty OF 250000, 24, TRUE, 25000)  -- a fine not exceeding $250,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (24 months) or both; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
        IF `the person is a corporation`
        THEN JUST (Penalty OF 250000, 0, FALSE, 25000)  -- a fine not exceeding $250,000, no imprisonment is stated, so 0; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an individual" and "in the case of a corporation" are the only cases the paragraphs name

-- src:30131 | (3) Any person to whom subsection (1) applies who —
-- src:30133 | (a) contravenes section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B
-- src:30134 | as applied by subsection (1); or
-- src:30136 | (b) in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or
-- src:30137 | 137B as applied by subsection (1), provides any
-- src:30142 | information which is false or misleading in a material
-- src:30143 | particular,
-- src:30145 | in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (2) shall be guilty
-- src:30146 | of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:30147 | $25,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:30148 | exceeding $2,500 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:30149 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 137U(3) (src:30131-30149)
GIVEN
    `the person contravened section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B as applied by section 137U(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person contravene section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B as applied by section 137U(1)?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B as applied by section 137U(1) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B as applied by section 137U(1), did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137U(3) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (3)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person contravened section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B as applied by section 137U(1)` OR `the person in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B as applied by section 137U(1) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("contravenes section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B as applied by subsection (1)"), not that anyone else is innocent
        IF ((`the person contravened section 135, 136(1) or (2), 137, 137A or 137B as applied by section 137U(1)` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`) OR (`the person in purported compliance with section 135, 136, 137 or 137B as applied by section 137U(1) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (i) "in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (2)": a case within subsection (2) is carved out of this one (a named complement)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 137U(3) (the penalty) (src:30131-30149)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 137U(3) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $25,000 and a further fine not exceeding $2,500 a day after conviction; no imprisonment is stated, so 0
    Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, 2500

-- src:30153 | (4) No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an
-- src:30154 | offence under this section after ––
-- src:30156 | (a) a court has made an order against the person for the
-- src:30157 | payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD in respect
-- src:30158 | of the same contravention; or
-- src:30160 | (b) the person has entered into an agreement with the
-- src:30161 | Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a
-- src:30162 | civil penalty under section 137ZD(4), in respect of the
-- src:30163 | same contravention.
@ref s 137U(4) (src:30153-30163)
GIVEN
    `a court has made an order for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention?
    `the person has agreed with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137U(4) no proceedings may be instituted for an offence under section 137U` MEANS
    IF `a court has made an order for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention` OR `the person has agreed with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an offence under this section after"
    -- MARGINAL-READING (b): the bar is limited by its own wording ("after"); outside the limit the other reading is NOTHING.

§ `s 137V: the trustee keeps a register of substantial unitholders`

-- src:30169 | 137V.—(1) The trustee of a real estate investment trust must keep a
-- src:30170 | register in which it must immediately enter —
@ref s 137V(1) (keeping the register) (src:30169-30170)
GIVEN
    `the body is the trustee of a real estate investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the trustee of a real estate investment trust within section 137S?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137V(1) the trustee must keep a register` MEANS
    IF `the body is the trustee of a real estate investment trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The trustee of a real estate investment trust must keep a register"; the body is not one

-- src:30169 | 137V.—(1) The trustee of a real estate investment trust must keep a
-- src:30170 | register in which it must immediately enter —
-- src:30172 | (a) the names of persons from whom it has received a notice
-- src:30173 | under section 135 as applied by section 137U(1); and
-- src:30175 | (b) against each name so entered, the information given in the
-- src:30176 | notice and, where it receives a notice under section 136 or
-- src:30177 | 137 as applied by section 137U(1), the information given
-- src:30178 | in that notice.
@ref s 137V(1) (entering the notice) (src:30169-30178)
GIVEN
    `the body is the trustee of a real estate investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the trustee of a real estate investment trust within section 137S?
    `the trustee has received a notice under section 135, 136 or 137 as applied by section 137U(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trustee received a notice under section 135, 136 or 137 as applied by section 137U(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137V(1) the trustee must immediately enter the names and information in the register` MEANS
    IF `the body is the trustee of a real estate investment trust` AND `the trustee has received a notice under section 135, 136 or 137 as applied by section 137U(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the names of persons from whom it has received a notice under section 135 as applied by section 137U(1)" and the information in a notice under section 136 or 137 as applied by section 137U(1)

DECLARE `s 137V action` IS ONE OF
    `s 137V enter the names and information in the register`
    `s 137V send the copy of the register`

-- "immediately" is read as a window of nought days (fork register A6): an entry on the day the notice is received is in time, one a day later is not.
-- src:30169 | 137V.—(1) The trustee of a real estate investment trust must keep a
-- src:30170 | register in which it must immediately enter —
-- src:30172 | (a) the names of persons from whom it has received a notice
-- src:30173 | under section 135 as applied by section 137U(1); and
-- src:30175 | (b) against each name so entered, the information given in the
-- src:30176 | notice and, where it receives a notice under section 136 or
-- src:30177 | 137 as applied by section 137U(1), the information given
-- src:30178 | in that notice.
@ref s 137V(1) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:30169-30178)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137V action`
`s 137V(1) the trustee must immediately enter the names and information in the register` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 137V enter the names and information in the register`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the names and information were not entered in the register immediately on receipt of the notice (section 137V(1))"

-- Subsection (2): where the register is kept. A register kept anywhere else is the text's no ("must keep").
-- src:30182 | (2) The trustee must keep the register at its registered office or, if
-- src:30183 | the trustee does not have a registered office, at its principal place of
-- src:30184 | business in Singapore, and the register must be open for inspection by
@ref s 137V(2) (the place) (src:30182-30184)
GIVEN
    `the trustee has a registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee have a registered office?
    `the register is kept at the registered office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the register kept at the corporation's registered office?
    `the register is kept at the principal place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the register kept at the corporation's principal place of business in Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137V(2) the register is kept at the place the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the trustee has a registered office`
    THEN IF `the register is kept at the registered office`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The trustee must keep the register at its registered office"
    ELSE IF `the register is kept at the principal place of business in Singapore`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the trustee does not have a registered office, at its principal place of business in Singapore"

-- Inspection: free to a unitholder; $2 "or such lesser sum as the trustee requires" for any other person, so $2 is the most that may be charged.
-- src:30182 | (2) The trustee must keep the register at its registered office or, if
-- src:30183 | the trustee does not have a registered office, at its principal place of
-- src:30184 | business in Singapore, and the register must be open for inspection by
-- src:30185 | a unitholder of the real estate investment trust without charge and by
-- src:30186 | any other person on payment for each inspection of a sum of $2 or
-- src:30187 | such lesser sum as the trustee requires.
@ref s 137V(2) (inspection) (src:30182-30187)
GIVEN
    `the person inspecting the register is a unitholder of the real estate investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who wants to inspect the register a unitholder of the real estate investment trust?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 137V(2) the most the trustee may charge for each inspection of the register, in Singapore dollars` MEANS
    IF `the person inspecting the register is a unitholder of the real estate investment trust`
    THEN 0  -- "without charge"
    ELSE 2  -- "a sum of $2 or such lesser sum as the trustee requires"

-- Subsection (3): copies. $1 a page or less, paid in advance; the copy to be sent within 14 days after the request, or such longer period as the Authority allows in the particular case.
-- src:30194 | (3) A person may request the trustee to provide the person with a
-- src:30195 | copy of the register or any part of the register on payment in advance
-- src:30196 | of a sum of $1 or such lesser sum as the trustee requires for every page
-- src:30197 | or part thereof required to be copied, and the trustee must send the
@ref s 137V(3) (the charge) (src:30194-30197)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 137V(3) the most the trustee may charge in advance for each page copied, in Singapore dollars` MEANS
    1  -- "a sum of $1 or such lesser sum as the trustee requires for every page or part thereof"

-- src:30197 | or part thereof required to be copied, and the trustee must send the
-- src:30198 | copy to that person within 14 days, or such longer period as the
-- src:30199 | Authority may allow in any particular case, after the day on which the
-- src:30200 | trustee received the request.
@ref s 137V(3) (the time) (src:30197-30200)
GIVEN
    `the day the trustee received the request for a copy` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the trustee receive the request for a copy of the register or part of it?
    `the Authority has allowed a longer period in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority allowed a longer period for sending the copy in this particular case?
    `the last day of the longer period the Authority has allowed` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the longer period the Authority has allowed (leave any date if none)?
GIVETH A DATE
`s 137V(3) the last day for the trustee to send the copy` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has allowed a longer period in the particular case` AND (`the last day of the longer period the Authority has allowed` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the trustee received the request for a copy` 14 Days)
    THEN `the last day of the longer period the Authority has allowed`
    ELSE `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the trustee received the request for a copy` 14 Days

-- src:30197 | or part thereof required to be copied, and the trustee must send the
-- src:30198 | copy to that person within 14 days, or such longer period as the
-- src:30199 | Authority may allow in any particular case, after the day on which the
-- src:30200 | trustee received the request.
@ref 2 s 137V(3) (in time) (src:30197-30200)
GIVEN
    `the day the trustee received the request for a copy` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the trustee receive the request for a copy of the register or part of it?
    `the Authority has allowed a longer period in the particular case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority allowed a longer period for sending the copy in this particular case?
    `the last day of the longer period the Authority has allowed` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the longer period the Authority has allowed (leave any date if none)?
    `the day the trustee sent the copy` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the trustee send the copy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137V(3) the copy is sent in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the trustee sent the copy` AT MOST `s 137V(3) the last day for the trustee to send the copy` `the day the trustee received the request for a copy` `the Authority has allowed a longer period in the particular case` `the last day of the longer period the Authority has allowed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the trustee must send the copy to that person within 14 days, or such longer period as the Authority may allow in any particular case"; a period fixed in the text's own words (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a))

-- The regulative rule counts days (the clock of a trace counts calendar days from the request).
-- src:30194 | (3) A person may request the trustee to provide the person with a
-- src:30195 | copy of the register or any part of the register on payment in advance
-- src:30196 | of a sum of $1 or such lesser sum as the trustee requires for every page
-- src:30197 | or part thereof required to be copied, and the trustee must send the
-- src:30198 | copy to that person within 14 days, or such longer period as the
-- src:30199 | Authority may allow in any particular case, after the day on which the
-- src:30200 | trustee received the request.
@ref s 137V(3) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:30194-30200)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137V action`
`s 137V(3) the trustee must send the copy within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 137V send the copy of the register`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the copy was not sent within 14 days after the request was received (section 137V(3))"

-- Subsection (4): the Authority's written requirement; the trustee sends the copy within 7 days after receiving it.
-- src:30204 | (4) The Authority may at any time in writing require the trustee to
-- src:30205 | provide it with a copy of the register or any part of the register and the
-- src:30206 | trustee must send the copy to the Authority within 7 days after the day
-- src:30207 | on which the trustee received the requirement.
@ref s 137V(4) (src:30204-30207)
GIVEN
    `the body is the trustee of a real estate investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the trustee of a real estate investment trust within section 137S?
    `the Authority has required the trustee in writing to provide a copy of the register or part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority required the trustee in writing to provide it with a copy of the register or part of it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137V(4) the trustee must send the Authority a copy of the register` MEANS
    IF `the body is the trustee of a real estate investment trust` AND `the Authority has required the trustee in writing to provide a copy of the register or part of it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Authority may at any time in writing require the trustee to provide it with a copy of the register or any part of the register and the trustee must send the copy"

-- src:30204 | (4) The Authority may at any time in writing require the trustee to
-- src:30205 | provide it with a copy of the register or any part of the register and the
-- src:30206 | trustee must send the copy to the Authority within 7 days after the day
-- src:30207 | on which the trustee received the requirement.
@ref 2 s 137V(4) (the time) (src:30204-30207)
GIVEN
    `the day the trustee received the Authority's requirement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the trustee receive the Authority's written requirement?
GIVETH A DATE
`s 137V(4) the last day for the trustee to send the copy to the Authority` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the trustee received the Authority's requirement` 7 Days

-- src:30204 | (4) The Authority may at any time in writing require the trustee to
-- src:30205 | provide it with a copy of the register or any part of the register and the
-- src:30206 | trustee must send the copy to the Authority within 7 days after the day
-- src:30207 | on which the trustee received the requirement.
@ref 2 s 137V(4) (in time) (src:30204-30207)
GIVEN
    `the day the trustee received the Authority's requirement` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the trustee receive the Authority's written requirement?
    `the day the trustee sent the copy` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the trustee send the copy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137V(4) the copy is sent to the Authority in time` MEANS
    IF `the day the trustee sent the copy` AT MOST `s 137V(4) the last day for the trustee to send the copy to the Authority` `the day the trustee received the Authority's requirement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the trustee must send the copy to the Authority within 7 days after the day on which the trustee received the requirement"; a period fixed in the text's own words (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (a))

-- src:30204 | (4) The Authority may at any time in writing require the trustee to
-- src:30205 | provide it with a copy of the register or any part of the register and the
-- src:30206 | trustee must send the copy to the Authority within 7 days after the day
-- src:30207 | on which the trustee received the requirement.
@ref s 137V(4) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:30204-30207)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137V action`
`s 137V(4) the trustee must send the Authority the copy within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 137V send the copy of the register`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the copy was not sent to the Authority within 7 days after the requirement was received (section 137V(4))"

-- src:30211 | (5) Any trustee which fails to comply with subsection (1), (2), (3) or
-- src:30212 | (4) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a
-- src:30213 | fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to
-- src:30214 | a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day
-- src:30215 | during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 137V(5) (src:30211-30215)
GIVEN
    `the trustee fails to comply with section 137V(1), (2), (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the trustee fail to comply with section 137V(1), (2), (3) or (4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137V(5) the trustee is guilty of an offence of failing to comply with the register provisions` MEANS
    IF `the trustee fails to comply with section 137V(1), (2), (3) or (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("Any trustee which fails to comply with subsection (1), (2), (3) or (4)"), not that a trustee that complies is innocent

-- src:30211 | (5) Any trustee which fails to comply with subsection (1), (2), (3) or
-- src:30212 | (4) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a
-- src:30213 | fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to
-- src:30214 | a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day
-- src:30215 | during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref 2 s 137V(5) (the penalty) (src:30211-30215)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 137V(5) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $50,000 and a further fine not exceeding $5,000 a day after conviction; no imprisonment is stated, so 0
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000


§ `s 137W: powers of the court with respect to non-compliance by substantial unitholders`

-- The orders of subsection (1), paragraphs (a) to (i). The kind matters in subsection (6), which carves out "an order restraining the exercise of voting rights" (paragraph (c));
-- fork register A7: paragraph (h), an order that the exercise of voting or other rights be disregarded, is not read as an order restraining their exercise.
DECLARE `s 137W(1) kind of order` IS ONE OF
    `s 137W(1)(a) an order restraining the substantial unitholder from disposing of any interest in the units`
    `s 137W(1)(b) an order restraining the holder or the person entitled to be the holder of the units from disposing of any interest in them`
    `s 137W(1)(c) an order restraining the exercise by any person of any voting or other rights attached to a unit`
    `s 137W(1)(d) an order directing the trustee not to make payment, or to defer making payment, of any sum due in respect of a unit`
    `s 137W(1)(e) an order directing the sale of any or all of the units`
    `s 137W(1)(f) an order directing the trustee not to register the transfer or transmission of units`
    `s 137W(1)(g) an order directing the Depository or any depository corporation not to register the transfer or transmission of units`
    `s 137W(1)(h) an order that any exercise of the voting or other rights attached to units be disregarded`
    `s 137W(1)(i) an order directing the trustee or any other person to do or refrain from doing an act to secure compliance with another order`

-- The court "may, on the application of the Authority": a "Where ..." condition and an application, on a function named for a power. SPLIT-SITE (ii), fork line B3:
-- the grant limit of the ruling of 2026-11-12 answers NOTHING when the gate fails; the periods ruling (b) would answer JUST FALSE. The same answer serves every paragraph (a) to (i).
-- src:30222 | 137W.—(1) Where a person is or has been a substantial unitholder
-- src:30223 | of a real estate investment trust and has failed to comply with
-- src:30224 | section 135, 136 or 137 as applied by section 137U(1), a court may,
-- src:30225 | on the application of the Authority, whether or not that failure still
-- src:30226 | continues, make one or more of the following orders:
@ref s 137W(1) (src:30222-30226)
GIVEN
    `the person is or has been a substantial unitholder of the real estate investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person, or has the person been, a substantial unitholder of the real estate investment trust?
    `the person has failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137 as applied by section 137U(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137 as applied by section 137U(1) (whether or not that failure still continues)?
    `the Authority has applied to the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority applied to the court for an order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137W(1) the court has power to make one or more of the orders listed in the subsection` MEANS
    IF `the person is or has been a substantial unitholder of the real estate investment trust` AND `the person has failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137 as applied by section 137U(1)` AND `the Authority has applied to the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (ii) "Where a person is or has been a substantial unitholder of a real estate investment trust and has failed to comply with section 135, 136 or 137 as applied by section 137U(1), a court may, on the application of the Authority"

-- src:30280 | (2) Any order made under this section may include such ancillary or
-- src:30281 | consequential provisions as the court thinks just.
@ref s 137W(2) (src:30280-30281)
GIVEN
    `an order has been made by the court under the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made an order under this section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137W(2) the order may include ancillary or consequential provisions the court thinks just` MEANS
    IF `an order has been made by the court under the section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any order made under this section may include such ancillary or consequential provisions as the court thinks just"

-- Subsection (3): a sale order may carry a condition against a sale to a person who is, or would become, a substantial unitholder.
-- src:30285 | (3) An order made under this section directing the sale of any unit
-- src:30286 | may provide that the sale is to be made within such time and subject
-- src:30287 | to such conditions (if any) as the court thinks fit, including, if the
-- src:30292 | court thinks fit, a condition that the sale must not be made to a person
-- src:30293 | who is, or, as a result of the sale, would become a substantial
-- src:30294 | unitholder of the real estate investment trust.
@ref s 137W(3) (src:30285-30294)
GIVEN
    `an order directing the sale of a unit has been made under the section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made an order directing the sale of a unit?
    `the court has made it a condition that the sale must not be made to a person who is, or would become, a substantial unitholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court made it a condition of the sale that it must not be made to a person who is, or as a result would become, a substantial unitholder of the business trust?
    `the buyer is, or as a result of the sale would become, a substantial unitholder of the real estate investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the buyer, or would the buyer as a result of the sale become, a substantial unitholder of the real estate investment trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137W(3) the sale to the buyer is barred by the court's condition` MEANS
    IF `an order directing the sale of a unit has been made under the section` AND `the court has made it a condition that the sale must not be made to a person who is, or would become, a substantial unitholder` AND `the buyer is, or as a result of the sale would become, a substantial unitholder of the real estate investment trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "including, if the court thinks fit, a condition that the sale must not be made to a person who is, or, as a result of the sale, would become a substantial unitholder of the real estate investment trust"

-- Subsection (4): where a unit is not sold, the Authority may apply for directions (SPLIT-SITE (ii): a "Where" gate on a function named for a power; fork line B4).
