§ `s 137X: power of a trustee to require disclosure of beneficial interest in its voting units`

-- Subsection (1): a power, so a gate that fails answers NOTHING (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12). The chapeau is one function; paragraphs (a) and (b) say what the notice may ask.
-- src:30358 | 137X.—(1) The trustee of a real estate investment trust may by
-- src:30359 | written notice require any unitholder of the trust within such
-- src:30360 | reasonable time as is specified in the notice —
@ref s 137X(1) (src:30358-30360)
GIVEN
    `the body is the trustee of a real estate investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the trustee of a real estate investment trust within section 137S?
    `the person is a unitholder of the real estate investment trust` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the keel's definition of "unitholder" answer for the person? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the requirement is made by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement made by written notice?
    `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify a time for the answer that is reasonable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137X(1) the trustee may require the unitholder to give the information` MEANS
    IF `the body is the trustee of a real estate investment trust` AND (`the person is a unitholder of the real estate investment trust` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the requirement is made by written notice` AND `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The trustee of a real estate investment trust may by written notice require any unitholder of the trust within such reasonable time as is specified in the notice"

