    IF `a notice has been issued to the person under section 137X(1), (2) or (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person to whom a notice is issued under subsection (1), (2) or (3)"

DECLARE `s 137X action` IS ONE OF
    `s 137X comply with the notice`

-- "Within such reasonable time as is specified in the notice": the number of days the notice allows is an input and the rule's window.
-- src:30358 | 137X.—(1) The trustee of a real estate investment trust may by
-- src:30359 | written notice require any unitholder of the trust within such
-- src:30360 | reasonable time as is specified in the notice —
-- src:30362 | (a) to inform it whether the unitholder holds any voting units
-- src:30363 | in the trust as beneficial owner or as trustee; and
-- src:30365 | (b) if the unitholder holds them as trustee, to indicate so far as
-- src:30366 | the unitholder can the persons for whom the unitholder
-- src:30367 | holds them (either by name or by other particulars
-- src:30368 | sufficient to enable those persons to be identified) and
-- src:30369 | the nature of their interest.
-- src:30373 | (2) Where the trustee of a real estate investment trust is informed
-- src:30374 | pursuant to a notice given to any person under subsection (1) or under
-- src:30375 | this subsection that any other person has an interest in any of the
-- src:30376 | voting units in the trust, the trustee may by written notice require that
-- src:30377 | other person within such reasonable time as is specified in the
-- src:30378 | notice —
-- src:30380 | (a) to inform it whether that other person holds that interest as
-- src:30381 | beneficial owner or as trustee; and
-- src:30383 | (b) if that other person holds it as trustee, to indicate so far as
-- src:30384 | that other person can the persons for whom that other
-- src:30385 | person holds it (either by name or by other particulars
-- src:30386 | sufficient to enable them to be identified) and the nature of
-- src:30387 | their interest.
-- src:30391 | (3) The trustee of a real estate investment trust may by written
-- src:30392 | notice require any unitholder of the trust to inform it, within such
-- src:30397 | reasonable time as is specified in the notice, whether any of the voting
-- src:30398 | rights carried by any voting units in the trust held by the unitholder
-- src:30399 | are the subject of an agreement or arrangement under which another
-- src:30400 | person is entitled to control the unitholder’s exercise of those rights
-- src:30401 | and, if so, to give particulars of the agreement or arrangement and the
-- src:30402 | parties to it.
-- src:30406 | (4) The notice referred to in subsection (1), (2) or (3) must contain
-- src:30407 | such other information as the Authority may prescribe, and the
-- src:30408 | delivery of such notice must comply with such requirements as the
-- src:30409 | Authority may prescribe.
-- src:30413 | (5) Any person to whom a notice is issued under subsection (1), (2)
-- src:30414 | or (3) must comply with that notice.
@ref s 137X(5) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:30358-30414)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party
    `the time the notice specifies, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the notice is the time that the notice specifies for the answer?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137X action`
`s 137X(5) the person must comply with the notice within the time it specifies` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 137X comply with the notice`
    WITHIN `the time the notice specifies, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the notice was not complied with within the time it specified (section 137X(5))"

-- Subsection (6): the trustee's duty to inscribe, "Whenever" counting as "where" (the ruling of 2026-11-05, (c)): a failed gate answers JUST FALSE.
-- src:30418 | (6) Whenever the trustee of a real estate investment trust receives
-- src:30419 | information from a person pursuant to a requirement imposed on the
-- src:30420 | person under this section with respect to units held by a unitholder of
-- src:30421 | the trust, it is under an obligation to inscribe against the name of that
-- src:30422 | unitholder in a separate part of the register kept by it under
-- src:30423 | section 137V —
-- src:30425 | (a) the fact that the requirement was imposed and the date on
-- src:30426 | which it was imposed; and
-- src:30428 | (b) the information received pursuant to the requirement.
@ref s 137X(6) (src:30418-30428)
GIVEN
    `the body is the trustee of a real estate investment trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the trustee of a real estate investment trust within section 137S?
    `the trustee has received information from a person pursuant to a requirement imposed under section 137X with respect to units held by a unitholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trustee received information from a person, pursuant to a requirement imposed on the person under section 137X, with respect to units held by a unitholder of the trustee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137X(6) the trustee must inscribe the fact of the requirement, its date and the information in a separate part of the register` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the body is the trustee of a real estate investment trust`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the trustee of a real estate investment trust"; the body is not one
        IF `the trustee has received information from a person pursuant to a requirement imposed under section 137X with respect to units held by a unitholder`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Whenever the trustee of a real estate investment trust receives information from a person pursuant to a requirement imposed on the person under this section with respect to units held by a unitholder of the trust"

-- src:30432 | (7) Section 137V applies in relation to the part of the register
-- src:30433 | referred to in subsection (6) as it applies in relation to the remainder
-- src:30434 | of the register and as if references to subsection (1) of that section
-- src:30435 | included references to subsection (6).
@ref s 137X(7) (src:30432-30435)
GIVEN
    `the part of the register is the separate part referred to in section 137X(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the part of the register the separate part that section 137X(6) refers to?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137X(7) section 137V applies to the separate part of the register` MEANS
    IF `the part of the register is the separate part referred to in section 137X(6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the part of the register referred to in subsection (6)"

-- src:30439 | (8) Any person who —
-- src:30441 | (a) intentionally or recklessly contravenes subsection (5); or
-- src:30443 | (b) in purported compliance with subsection (5), provides any
-- src:30444 | information which the person knows is false or misleading
-- src:30445 | in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is,
-- src:30450 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall —
-- src:30452 | (c) in the case of an individual, be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:30453 | not exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:30454 | exceeding 2 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:30455 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $25,000 for every
-- src:30456 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues
-- src:30457 | after conviction; or
-- src:30459 | (d) in the case of a corporation, be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:30460 | not exceeding $250,000 and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:30461 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $25,000 for every
-- src:30462 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues
-- src:30463 | after conviction.
@ref s 137X(8) (src:30439-30463)
GIVEN
    `the person contravened section 137X(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person contravene section 137X(5)?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance with section 137X(5) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 137X(5), did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137X(8) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (8)` MEANS
    IF ((`the person contravened section 137X(5)` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`) OR (`the person in purported compliance with section 137X(5) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("intentionally or recklessly contravenes subsection (5)" or "provides any information which the person knows is false or misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is"), not that anyone else is innocent

@ref s 137X(8) (the penalty) (src:30439-30463)
GIVEN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 137X(8) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an individual`
        THEN JUST (Penalty OF 250000, 24, TRUE, 25000)  -- a fine not exceeding $250,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (24 months) or both; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
        IF `the person is a corporation`
        THEN JUST (Penalty OF 250000, 0, FALSE, 25000)  -- a fine not exceeding $250,000, no imprisonment is stated, so 0; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an individual" and "in the case of a corporation" are the only cases the paragraphs name

-- src:30467 | (9) Any person who —
-- src:30469 | (a) contravenes subsection (5); or
-- src:30471 | (b) in purported compliance with subsection (5), provides any
-- src:30472 | information which is false or misleading in a material
-- src:30473 | particular,
-- src:30475 | in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (8) shall be guilty
-- src:30476 | of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:30477 | $25,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:30478 | exceeding $2,500 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:30479 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 137X(9) (src:30467-30479)
GIVEN
    `the person contravened section 137X(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person contravene section 137X(5)?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance with section 137X(5) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 137X(5), did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137X(9) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (9)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person contravened section 137X(5)` OR `the person in purported compliance with section 137X(5) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("contravenes subsection (5)"), not that anyone else is innocent
        IF ((`the person contravened section 137X(5)` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`) OR (`the person in purported compliance with section 137X(5) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (i) "in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (8)": a case within subsection (8) is carved out of this one (a named complement)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 137X(9) (the penalty) (src:30467-30479)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 137X(9) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- a fine not exceeding $25,000 and a further fine not exceeding $2,500 a day after conviction; no imprisonment is stated, so 0
    Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, 2500

-- src:30491 | (11) No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an
-- src:30492 | offence under this section after ––
-- src:30494 | (a) a court has made an order against the person for the
-- src:30495 | payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD in respect
-- src:30496 | of the same contravention; or
-- src:30501 | (b) the person has entered into an agreement with the
-- src:30502 | Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a
-- src:30503 | civil penalty under section 137ZD(4), in respect of the
-- src:30504 | same contravention.
@ref s 137X(11) (src:30491-30504)
GIVEN
    `a court has made an order for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order against the person for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention?
    `the person has agreed with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137X(11) no proceedings may be instituted for an offence under section 137X` MEANS
    IF `a court has made an order for the payment of a civil penalty under section 137ZD for the same contravention` OR `the person has agreed with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 137ZD(4) for the same contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No proceedings shall be instituted against a person for an offence under this section after"
    -- MARGINAL-READING (b): the bar is limited by its own wording ("after"); outside the limit the other reading is NOTHING.

-- Subsection (10): the defence. It is limited to the paragraphs that are contraventions of subsection (5), (8)(a) and (9)(a), and is a defence "if the person proves"
-- one of two things. When neither is proved the answer is JUST FALSE, worded "this section gives no defence on these facts" (NOTHINGBURGER, (b)).
-- src:30483 | (10) A person shall not be guilty of an offence under
-- src:30484 | subsection (8)(a) or (9)(a) if the person proves that the information
-- src:30485 | in question was already in the possession of the trustee of the real
-- src:30486 | estate investment trust, or that the requirement to give it was for any
-- src:30487 | other reason frivolous or vexatious.
@ref s 137X(10) (src:30483-30487)
GIVEN
    `the offence charged is one under section 137X(8)(a) or (9)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offence charged one under section 137X(8)(a) or (9)(a) (a contravention of section 137X(5)), and not one for false or misleading information?
    `the person proves that the information in question was already in the possession of the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person prove that the information in question was already in the possession of the trustee?
    `the person proves that the requirement to give the information was for any other reason frivolous or vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person prove that the requirement to give the information was, for any other reason, frivolous or vexatious?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137X(10) the person is not guilty of an offence under subsection (8)(a) or (9)(a)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence charged is one under section 137X(8)(a) or (9)(a)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under subsection (8)(a) or (9)(a)"
        IF `the person proves that the information in question was already in the possession of the trustee` OR `the person proves that the requirement to give the information was for any other reason frivolous or vexatious`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person proves that the information in question was already in the possession of the trustee of the real estate investment trust, or that the requirement to give it was for any other reason frivolous or vexatious"; this section gives no defence on these facts

